IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sssa-nouns`
IMPORT `sssa-part3-administration`

-- Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 1 December 2025 -- LAYER 1, PART 4: MISCELLANEOUS.
--
-- Offences (ss 11, 14(4), 15), the court's order and the certificate (ss 12, 13),
-- the power to obtain information (s 14), bodies corporate (s 16), composition
-- (s 17), prosecutions (s 18), personal liability (s 19) and regulations (s 20).
--
-- Every offence answers JUST TRUE or NOTHING: an unmet element does not say the
-- person is innocent of anything, only that this provision does not reach them.
-- The ceiling of a penalty is checked with `a sentence is within the ceiling of a
-- penalty` from sssa-part3-administration.l4.

§ `Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 -- Part 4 -- Miscellaneous`

§§ `s 11 Obtaining benefit through false or misleading statements, etc.`

-- s 11(1): a person (a) who knowingly or recklessly makes a false or misleading
-- statement, or produces or provides a document known or reasonably ought to be
-- known to be false in a material particular; and (b) who, with the intention of
-- dishonestly inducing another person to accept it as genuine, dishonestly obtains
-- a cash grant or other benefit.
-- src:570 | 11.—(1) A person —
-- src:572 | (a) who —
-- src:574 | (i) knowingly or recklessly makes any false or
-- src:575 | misleading statement; or
-- src:577 | (ii) produces or provides, or causes to be produced or
-- src:578 | provided, any document which the person knows, or
-- src:579 | ought reasonably to know, is false in a material
-- src:580 | particular; and
-- src:582 | (b) who, with the intention of dishonestly inducing another
-- src:583 | person to accept the statement or document as genuine,
-- src:588 | dishonestly obtains any cash grant or other benefit under
-- src:589 | the Scheme,
-- src:591 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:592 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:593 | 12 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 11(1) (src:570-593)
GIVEN `the person knowingly or recklessly makes a false or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person produces or provides, or causes to be produced or provided, a document which the person knows, or ought reasonably to know, is false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person dishonestly obtains a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme, with the intention of dishonestly inducing another person to accept the statement or document as genuine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF (`the person knowingly or recklessly makes a false or misleading statement`
        OR `the person produces or provides, or causes to be produced or provided, a document which the person knows, or ought reasonably to know, is false in a material particular`)
       AND `the person dishonestly obtains a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme, with the intention of dishonestly inducing another person to accept the statement or document as genuine`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of "A person" who does both (a) and (b), and the subsection says nothing of any other conduct
    ELSE NOTHING

-- fields:                                greatest fine in dollars, greatest imprisonment in months
-- src:588 | dishonestly obtains any cash grant or other benefit under
-- src:589 | the Scheme,
-- src:591 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:592 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:593 | 12 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 11(1) (src:588-593)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 11(1) the greatest penalty` MEANS Penalty OF 5000, 12

-- src:588 | dishonestly obtains any cash grant or other benefit under
-- src:589 | the Scheme,
-- src:591 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:592 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:593 | 12 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 11(1) (src:588-593)
GIVEN fine IS A NUMBER
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(1) the sentence is within the greatest penalty` MEANS
    IF `a sentence is within the ceiling of a penalty` (`s 11(1) the greatest penalty`) fine months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 11(2): "Subsection (1) does not affect any right of recovery under section 10."
-- src:595 | (2) Subsection (1) does not affect any right of recovery under
-- src:596 | section 10.
@ref SSSA2015 s 11(2) (src:595-596)
GIVEN `the person is convicted under section 11(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a right of recovery under section 10` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(2) the right of recovery under section 10 is unaffected by section 11(1)` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted under section 11(1)` AND `there is a right of recovery under section 10`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of how "Subsection (1)" bears on "any right of recovery under section 10"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 12 Recovery of cash grant, etc., upon conviction`

-- s 12: where a person has received a cash grant or other benefit and is convicted
-- of an offence under the Act in connection with it, the court "may, in addition to
-- imposing any penalty prescribed for the offence, order that the person pay to an
-- administrator the amount certified by the administrator".
-- src:598 | Recovery of cash grant, etc., upon conviction
-- src:600 | 12. Where —
-- src:602 | (a) a person has received any cash grant or other benefit under
-- src:603 | the Scheme; and
-- src:605 | (b) the person is convicted of an offence under this Act in
-- src:606 | connection with the cash grant or other benefit,
-- src:608 | the court before which the conviction is had may, in addition to
-- src:609 | imposing any penalty prescribed for the offence, order that the person
-- src:610 | pay to an administrator the amount certified by the administrator to be
-- src:611 | recoverable from the person, as at the date of the conviction, in
-- src:612 | respect of the cash grant or other benefit.
@ref SSSA2015 s 12 (src:598-612)
GIVEN `the person has received a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is convicted of an offence under this Act in connection with the cash grant or other benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12 the court may order the person to pay the certified amount to an administrator` MEANS
    IF `the person has received a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme`
       AND `the person is convicted of an offence under this Act in connection with the cash grant or other benefit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the order is for a person who "has received" the cash grant or benefit and "is convicted of an offence under this Act in connection with" it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:598 | Recovery of cash grant, etc., upon conviction
-- src:600 | 12. Where —
-- src:602 | (a) a person has received any cash grant or other benefit under
-- src:603 | the Scheme; and
-- src:605 | (b) the person is convicted of an offence under this Act in
-- src:606 | connection with the cash grant or other benefit,
-- src:608 | the court before which the conviction is had may, in addition to
-- src:609 | imposing any penalty prescribed for the offence, order that the person
-- src:610 | pay to an administrator the amount certified by the administrator to be
-- src:611 | recoverable from the person, as at the date of the conviction, in
-- src:612 | respect of the cash grant or other benefit.
@ref SSSA2015 s 12 (src:598-612)
GIVEN `the person has received a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is convicted of an offence under this Act in connection with the cash grant or other benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount certified by the administrator to be recoverable from the person as at the date of the conviction` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 12 the amount the court may order the person to pay` MEANS
    IF `the person has received a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme`
       AND `the person is convicted of an offence under this Act in connection with the cash grant or other benefit`
    THEN `the amount certified by the administrator to be recoverable from the person as at the date of the conviction`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the order is for "the amount certified by the administrator to be recoverable from the person, as at the date of the conviction"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 13 Certificate on amount of cash grant, etc.`

-- s 13: a certificate "purporting to be issued by an administrator" certifying
-- (a) the amount received as at a date, or (b) the amount recoverable as at a date,
-- "is prima facie evidence" of it.  Prima facie evidence is not conclusive; the
-- section says no more.
-- src:614 | Certificate on amount of cash grant, etc.
-- src:616 | 13. In any proceedings before any court, tribunal or authority
-- src:617 | (including any proceedings for the recovery of any cash grant or other
-- src:618 | benefit under the Scheme), a certificate purporting to be issued by an
-- src:619 | administrator certifying —
-- src:621 | (a) the amount of any cash grant or other benefit under the
-- src:622 | Scheme received by any person as at any date; or
-- src:624 | (b) the amount recoverable from any person as at any date in
-- src:625 | respect of any cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme
-- src:626 | received by that person,
-- src:628 | is prima facie evidence that the amount so stated was received by that
-- src:629 | person or is recoverable from that person (as the case may be) as at
-- src:630 | that date.
@ref SSSA2015 s 13 (src:614-630)
GIVEN `the certificate purports to be issued by an administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate certifies the amount of a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme received by a person as at a date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate certifies the amount recoverable from a person as at a date in respect of a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 the certificate is prima facie evidence of the amount stated` MEANS
    IF `the certificate purports to be issued by an administrator`
       AND (`the certificate certifies the amount of a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme received by a person as at a date`
            OR `the certificate certifies the amount recoverable from a person as at a date in respect of a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section is about "a certificate purporting to be issued by an administrator certifying" an amount received or an amount recoverable
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 14 Power to obtain information`

-- s 14(1): the Commissioner, for the purpose of reviewing the administration of the
-- Scheme or the disbursement or conferment of a benefit, or an investigator, for the
-- purpose of conducting an investigation under the Act, may (a) by written notice
-- require a person to attend at a reasonable time and place to answer a question or
-- give a signed statement; (b) require a person (i) to provide information within the
-- person's knowledge, or (ii) to produce a document or record for inspection; (c)
-- retain the original of a document or record, or make copies, "that the Commissioner
-- or investigator (as the case may be) believes on reasonable grounds to be
-- connected with the disbursement or conferment of any benefit under the Scheme".
-- FORK F-3: the closing words of (b), which the converter renders as a second
-- "(b)" line (src:657-660), are read as qualifying both (b)(i) and (b)(ii).
-- src:637 | 14.—(1) The Commissioner may, for the purpose of reviewing the
-- src:638 | administration of the Scheme or the disbursement or conferment of
-- src:639 | any benefit under the Scheme, or an investigator may, for the purpose
-- src:640 | of conducting any investigation under this Act —
-- src:642 | (a) by written notice require any person to attend at such
-- src:643 | reasonable time and at such place as may be specified by
-- src:644 | the Commissioner or investigator (as the case may be) to
-- src:645 | answer any question or to provide a signed statement in
-- src:646 | writing concerning the disbursement or conferment of any
-- src:647 | benefit under the Scheme;
-- src:649 | (b) require any person —
-- src:651 | (i) to provide any information within the person’s
-- src:652 | knowledge; or
-- src:654 | (ii) to produce for inspection any document or record in
-- src:655 | the person’s possession,
-- src:657 | (b) that the Commissioner or investigator (as the case may be)
-- src:658 | believes on reasonable grounds to be connected with the
-- src:659 | disbursement or conferment of any benefit under the
-- src:660 | Scheme; and
-- src:662 | (c) retain the original of any document or record that the
-- src:663 | Commissioner or investigator (as the case may be) believes
-- src:664 | on reasonable grounds to be connected with the
-- src:665 | disbursement or conferment of any benefit under the
-- src:666 | Scheme, or make or cause to be made, without payment,
-- src:667 | copies of or extracts from that document or record.
@ref SSSA2015 s 14(1) (src:637-667)
GIVEN requirer IS A `Person requiring`
      purpose IS A `Purpose of the requirement`
      thing IS A `Thing required`
      `a written notice is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time and place specified are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question or statement concerns the disbursement or conferment of any benefit under the Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirer believes on reasonable grounds that the information, document or record is connected with the disbursement or conferment of any benefit under the Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(1) the requirer may make the requirement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the requirer has the purpose that section 14(1) gives`
           AND thing EQUALS `to attend, answer a question or give a signed statement`
           AND `a written notice is given`
           AND `the time and place specified are reasonable`
           AND `the question or statement concerns the disbursement or conferment of any benefit under the Scheme`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the requirer has the purpose that section 14(1) gives`
           AND NOT (thing EQUALS `to attend, answer a question or give a signed statement`)
           AND `the requirer believes on reasonable grounds that the information, document or record is connected with the disbursement or conferment of any benefit under the Scheme`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is the Commissioner's "for the purpose of reviewing the administration of the Scheme or the disbursement or conferment of any benefit" or an investigator's "for the purpose of conducting any investigation under this Act", and is exercised "by written notice" at a "reasonable time" for (a) or on the belief "on reasonable grounds" for (b) and (c)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the requirer has the purpose that section 14(1) gives` MEANS
            (requirer EQUALS `the Commissioner` AND purpose EQUALS `reviewing the administration of the Scheme or the disbursement or conferment of a benefit`)
            OR (requirer EQUALS `an investigator as requirer` AND purpose EQUALS `conducting an investigation under this Act`)

-- s 14(2)(a): where a document or record required is kept in electronic form, the
-- power to require it to be produced for inspection under s 14(1)(b)(ii) includes
-- the power to require it in legible form.
-- src:669 | (2) Where any document or record required by the Commissioner
-- src:670 | or an investigator is kept in electronic form, then —
-- src:672 | (a) the power of the Commissioner or investigator (as the case
-- src:673 | may be) to require that document or record to be produced
-- src:674 | for inspection under subsection (1)(b)(ii) includes the
-- src:675 | power to require that document or record to be produced
-- src:676 | for inspection in legible form; and
@ref SSSA2015 s 14(2)(a) (src:669-676)
GIVEN requirer IS A `Person requiring`
      thing IS A `Thing required`
      `the document or record is kept in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(2)(a) the power to require production includes the power to require it in legible form` MEANS
    IF (requirer EQUALS `the Commissioner` OR requirer EQUALS `an investigator as requirer`)
       AND thing EQUALS `to produce a document or record for inspection`
       AND `the document or record is kept in electronic form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about a document or record "required by the Commissioner or an investigator" that "is kept in electronic form" and is to be "produced for inspection"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 14(2)(b): subsection (1)(c) applies to any copy so made available.
-- src:681 | (b) subsection (1)(c) applies to any copy of that document or
-- src:682 | record so made available.
@ref SSSA2015 s 14(2)(b) (src:681-682)
GIVEN `the document or record is kept in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the document or record has been made available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(2)(b) section 14(1)(c) applies to the copy` MEANS
    IF `the document or record is kept in electronic form` AND `a copy of the document or record has been made available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph applies to "any copy of that document or record so made available"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 14(3): a copy or extract made under s 14(1)(c) and certified as such by the
-- Commissioner or an investigator is admissible as evidence in any proceedings
-- under the Act.
-- src:684 | (3) Any copy of or extract from any document or record made under
-- src:685 | subsection (1)(c) and certified as such by the Commissioner or an
-- src:686 | investigator is admissible as evidence in any proceedings under this
-- src:687 | Act.
@ref SSSA2015 s 14(3) (src:684-687)
GIVEN `the copy or extract was made under section 14(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      certifier IS A `Person requiring`
      `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(3) the copy or extract is admissible as evidence` MEANS
    IF `the copy or extract was made under section 14(1)(c)`
       AND (certifier EQUALS `the Commissioner` OR certifier EQUALS `an investigator as requirer`)
       AND `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the copy is admissible if "made under subsection (1)(c) and certified as such by the Commissioner or an investigator", "in any proceedings under this Act"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 14(4): the time allowed.  A person who provides or produces on or before the
-- last day allowed is within the time (FORK F-4: "within the time allowed" includes
-- the last day).  The count is of days from the requirement to the day the person
-- provided or produced it, or to the day asked about if the person has not.
-- src:689 | (4) Any person who, when required by the Commissioner or an
-- src:690 | investigator under subsection (1)(b) to provide any information or
-- src:691 | produce any document or record, refuses or fails, without reasonable
-- src:692 | excuse, to do so within the time allowed by the Commissioner or
-- src:693 | investigator (as the case may be) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:694 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:695 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 14(4) (src:689-695)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed by the Commissioner or investigator` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days counted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(4) the person is within the time allowed` MEANS
    IF `the number of days counted` AT MOST `the number of days allowed by the Commissioner or investigator`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the time allowed by the Commissioner or investigator"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:689 | (4) Any person who, when required by the Commissioner or an
-- src:690 | investigator under subsection (1)(b) to provide any information or
-- src:691 | produce any document or record, refuses or fails, without reasonable
-- src:692 | excuse, to do so within the time allowed by the Commissioner or
-- src:693 | investigator (as the case may be) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:694 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:695 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 14(4) (src:689-695)
GIVEN requirer IS A `Person requiring`
      `the requirement was made under section 14(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days allowed by the Commissioner or investigator` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days counted` IS A NUMBER
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(4) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF (requirer EQUALS `the Commissioner` OR requirer EQUALS `an investigator as requirer`)
       AND `the requirement was made under section 14(1)(b)`
       AND (`the person refused`
            OR `s 14(4) the person is within the time allowed` `the number of days allowed by the Commissioner or investigator` `the number of days counted` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
       AND NOT `the person has a reasonable excuse`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of a person "required by the Commissioner or an investigator under subsection (1)(b)" who "refuses or fails, without reasonable excuse, to do so within the time allowed"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- fields:                                greatest fine in dollars, greatest imprisonment in months
-- src:689 | (4) Any person who, when required by the Commissioner or an
-- src:690 | investigator under subsection (1)(b) to provide any information or
-- src:691 | produce any document or record, refuses or fails, without reasonable
-- src:692 | excuse, to do so within the time allowed by the Commissioner or
-- src:693 | investigator (as the case may be) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:694 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:695 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 14(4) (src:689-695)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 14(4) the greatest penalty` MEANS Penalty OF 10000, 6

-- src:689 | (4) Any person who, when required by the Commissioner or an
-- src:690 | investigator under subsection (1)(b) to provide any information or
-- src:691 | produce any document or record, refuses or fails, without reasonable
-- src:692 | excuse, to do so within the time allowed by the Commissioner or
-- src:693 | investigator (as the case may be) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:694 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:695 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 14(4) (src:689-695)
GIVEN fine IS A NUMBER
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(4) the sentence is within the greatest penalty` MEANS
    IF `a sentence is within the ceiling of a penalty` (`s 14(4) the greatest penalty`) fine months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The duty behind s 14(4) as a regulative rule: the person required must provide
-- the information or produce the document or record within the time allowed.  The
-- time allowed is the requirer's, so it is a parameter in days.
-- src:689 | (4) Any person who, when required by the Commissioner or an
-- src:690 | investigator under subsection (1)(b) to provide any information or
-- src:691 | produce any document or record, refuses or fails, without reasonable
-- src:692 | excuse, to do so within the time allowed by the Commissioner or
-- src:693 | investigator (as the case may be) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:694 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:695 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 14(4) (src:689-695)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed by the Commissioner or investigator` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party under the Act` `An act under the Act`
`s 14(4) duty of the person required` MEANS
    PARTY `the person required`
    MUST `provide the information or produce the document or record`
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed by the Commissioner or investigator`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person required` BECAUSE "the person required did not provide the information or produce the document or record within the time allowed"

-- EXPECT FULFILLED: 7 days allowed; provided on day 6.
#TRACE `s 14(4) duty of the person required` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person required` DOES `provide the information or produce the document or record` AT 6
-- EXPECT FULFILLED: provided on day 7, the last day allowed (FORK F-4).
#TRACE `s 14(4) duty of the person required` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person required` DOES `provide the information or produce the document or record` AT 7
-- EXPECT BREACH: provided on day 8 (BREACH BY the person required).
#TRACE `s 14(4) duty of the person required` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person required` DOES `provide the information or produce the document or record` AT 8
-- EXPECT PENDING: nothing done by day 7; still outstanding with no time left (WITHIN 0).
#TRACE `s 14(4) duty of the person required` 7 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 7)
-- EXPECT BREACH: nothing done by day 8 (BREACH BY the person required).
#TRACE `s 14(4) duty of the person required` 7 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 8)

§§ `s 15 Obstructing Commissioner or investigator in execution of duties`

-- src:697 | Obstructing Commissioner or investigator in execution of
-- src:698 | duties
-- src:700 | 15. Any person who, without reasonable excuse, obstructs, hinders
-- src:701 | or impedes the Commissioner or an investigator in the performance
-- src:702 | or execution of a duty or anything which the Commissioner or
-- src:703 | investigator (as the case may be) is authorised, empowered or
-- src:704 | required to do under this Act shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:705 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to
-- src:706 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 15 (src:697-706)
GIVEN obstructed IS A `Person requiring`
      `the person obstructs, hinders or impedes the Commissioner or the investigator in the performance or execution of a duty or anything the Commissioner or investigator is authorised, empowered or required to do under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF (obstructed EQUALS `the Commissioner` OR obstructed EQUALS `an investigator as requirer`)
       AND `the person obstructs, hinders or impedes the Commissioner or the investigator in the performance or execution of a duty or anything the Commissioner or investigator is authorised, empowered or required to do under this Act`
       AND NOT `the person has a reasonable excuse`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is to obstruct, hinder or impede "the Commissioner or an investigator", "without reasonable excuse"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- fields:                                greatest fine in dollars, greatest imprisonment in months
