-- src:703 | investigator (as the case may be) is authorised, empowered or
-- src:704 | required to do under this Act shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:705 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to
-- src:706 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 15 (src:697-706)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 15 the greatest penalty` MEANS Penalty OF 20000, 12

-- src:697 | Obstructing Commissioner or investigator in execution of
-- src:698 | duties
-- src:700 | 15. Any person who, without reasonable excuse, obstructs, hinders
-- src:701 | or impedes the Commissioner or an investigator in the performance
-- src:702 | or execution of a duty or anything which the Commissioner or
-- src:703 | investigator (as the case may be) is authorised, empowered or
-- src:704 | required to do under this Act shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:705 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to
-- src:706 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 15 (src:697-706)
GIVEN fine IS A NUMBER
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 the sentence is within the greatest penalty` MEANS
    IF `a sentence is within the ceiling of a penalty` (`s 15 the greatest penalty`) fine months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `The offences of the Act together`

-- The greatest penalty for each offence the Act creates, gathered so that a caller
-- can ask for it by offence: s 8(6), s 9(7), s 11(1), s 14(4) and s 15.  Each
-- ceiling is the constant defined at its own section above.
-- src:400 | (6) Any person who does any act in contravention of subsection (3)
-- src:401 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:402 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:403 | 12 months or to both.
-- src:514 | (7) Any person who does any act in contravention of subsection (2),
-- src:515 | (3) or (5) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:516 | to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:517 | exceeding 12 months or to both.
-- src:588 | dishonestly obtains any cash grant or other benefit under
-- src:589 | the Scheme,
-- src:591 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:592 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:593 | 12 months or to both.
-- src:689 | (4) Any person who, when required by the Commissioner or an
-- src:690 | investigator under subsection (1)(b) to provide any information or
-- src:691 | produce any document or record, refuses or fails, without reasonable
-- src:692 | excuse, to do so within the time allowed by the Commissioner or
-- src:693 | investigator (as the case may be) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:694 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:695 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both.
-- src:700 | 15. Any person who, without reasonable excuse, obstructs, hinders
-- src:701 | or impedes the Commissioner or an investigator in the performance
-- src:702 | or execution of a duty or anything which the Commissioner or
-- src:703 | investigator (as the case may be) is authorised, empowered or
-- src:704 | required to do under this Act shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:705 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to
-- src:706 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 ss 8(6), 9(7), 11(1), 14(4) and 15 (src:400-403) (src:514-517) (src:588-593) (src:689-695) (src:700-706)
GIVEN offence IS AN `Offence under the Act`
GIVETH A Penalty
`ss 8(6), 9(7), 11(1), 14(4) and 15 the greatest penalty for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `the offence in section 8(6)` THEN `s 8(6) the greatest penalty`
    WHEN `the offence in section 9(7)` THEN `s 9(7) the greatest penalty`
    WHEN `the offence in section 11(1)` THEN `s 11(1) the greatest penalty`
    WHEN `the offence in section 14(4)` THEN `s 14(4) the greatest penalty`
    WHEN `the offence in section 15` THEN `s 15 the greatest penalty`

§§ `s 16 Offences by bodies corporate, etc.`

-- s 16(5) "body corporate" includes a limited liability partnership as defined in
-- section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005.  "includes" does
-- not close the list, so another kind of entity is not answered.
-- src:755 | (5) In this section —
-- src:757 | “body corporate” includes a limited liability partnership as
-- src:758 | defined in section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships
-- src:759 | Act 2005;
-- src:761 | “officer” —
-- src:763 | (a) in relation to a body corporate, means any director,
-- src:764 | partner, member of the board of management, chief
-- src:765 | executive, manager, secretary or other similar officer
-- src:766 | of the body corporate, and includes any person
-- src:767 | purporting to act in any such capacity; or
-- src:769 | (b) in relation to an unincorporated association (other
-- src:770 | than a partnership), means the president, the
-- src:771 | secretary, or any member of the committee of the
-- src:772 | unincorporated association, or any person holding a
-- src:777 | position analogous to that of president, secretary or
-- src:778 | member of such a committee, and includes any
-- src:779 | person purporting to act in any such capacity;
-- src:781 | “partner” includes a person purporting to act as a partner.
@ref SSSA2015 s 16(5) "body corporate" (src:755-781)
GIVEN entity IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(5) the entity is a body corporate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF entity EQUALS `an ordinary body corporate`
           OR entity EQUALS `a limited liability partnership as defined in section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "body corporate" "includes" a limited liability partnership and the definition does not say it includes no other entity
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 16(5) "officer" in relation to a body corporate: any director, partner, member
-- of the board of management, chief executive, manager, secretary or other similar
-- officer, and includes any person purporting to act in any such capacity.
