@ref SSSA2015 s 16(5) "partner" (src:781-781)
GIVEN `the person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person purports to act as a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(5) the person is a partner` MEANS
    IF `the person is a partner` OR `the person purports to act as a partner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "partner" "includes" a person purporting to act as a partner, and the definition does not say who else is a partner
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 16(1): the officer of a body corporate whose offence was committed with the
-- officer's consent or connivance, or is attributable to the officer's neglect, is
-- guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate.
-- src:710 | 16.—(1) Where an offence under this Act committed by a body
-- src:711 | corporate is proved —
-- src:713 | (a) to have been committed with the consent or connivance of
-- src:714 | an officer; or
-- src:716 | (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the officer’s part,
-- src:718 | the officer as well as the body corporate shall be guilty of the offence
-- src:719 | and shall be liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
-- src:721 | (2) Where the affairs of a body corporate are managed by its
-- src:722 | members, subsection (1) is to apply in relation to the acts and defaults
@ref SSSA2015 s 16(1) (src:710-722)
GIVEN entity IS A `Kind of entity`
      `an offence under this Act committed by the body corporate is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
      position IS A `Position in a body corporate`
      `the offence was committed with the consent or connivance of the officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is attributable to neglect on the officer's part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(1) the officer is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` MEANS
    IF `s 16(5) the entity is a body corporate` entity EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `an offence under this Act committed by the body corporate is proved`
       AND `s 16(5)(a) the person is an officer of a body corporate` position EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (`the offence was committed with the consent or connivance of the officer` OR `the offence is attributable to neglect on the officer's part`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the officer is guilty where the offence by the body corporate "is proved" to have been committed with "the consent or connivance of an officer" or to be attributable to "neglect"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 16(2): where the affairs of a body corporate are managed by its members,
-- subsection (1) applies to the acts and defaults of a member in connection with
-- the member's functions of management as if the member were a director.
-- src:721 | (2) Where the affairs of a body corporate are managed by its
-- src:722 | members, subsection (1) is to apply in relation to the acts and defaults
-- src:727 | of a member in connection with the member’s functions of
-- src:728 | management as if the member were a director of the body corporate.
@ref SSSA2015 s 16(2) (src:721-728)
GIVEN `the affairs of the body corporate are managed by its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or default is of a member in connection with the member's functions of management` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(2) section 16(1) applies to the member as if the member were a director` MEANS
    IF `the affairs of the body corporate are managed by its members`
       AND `the act or default is of a member in connection with the member's functions of management`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about a body corporate whose "affairs ... are managed by its members" and a member's acts and defaults "in connection with the member’s functions of management"
    ELSE NOTHING

