    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 17 Composition of offences`

-- s 17(1): the Board, or an officer or employee of the Board authorised by the
-- Board in writing, may compound an offence that is prescribed as compoundable, by
-- collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having committed it a sum not
-- exceeding the lower of (a) one half of the maximum fine prescribed for the offence
-- and (b) $1,000.  Which offences are prescribed as compoundable is in regulations
-- that are not among the sources, so it is an input.
-- src:785 | 17.—(1) The Board, or an officer or employee of the Board who is
-- src:786 | authorised by the Board in writing, may compound any offence under
-- src:787 | this Act that is prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting
-- src:788 | from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence
-- src:789 | a sum not exceeding the lower of the following:
-- src:791 | (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is
-- src:792 | prescribed for the offence;
-- src:794 | (b) $1,000.
@ref SSSA2015 s 17(1) (src:785-794)
GIVEN compounder IS A `Who compounds`
      `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is reasonably suspected of having committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) the Board or its authorised officer or employee may compound the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (compounder EQUALS `the Board` OR compounder EQUALS `an officer or employee of the Board who is authorised by the Board in writing`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given to "The Board, or an officer or employee of the Board who is authorised by the Board in writing"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `the person is reasonably suspected of having committed the offence`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sum is collected "from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which offences are "prescribed as a compoundable offence" is in regulations that are not among the sources
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:785 | 17.—(1) The Board, or an officer or employee of the Board who is
-- src:786 | authorised by the Board in writing, may compound any offence under
-- src:787 | this Act that is prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting
-- src:788 | from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence
-- src:789 | a sum not exceeding the lower of the following:
-- src:791 | (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is
-- src:792 | prescribed for the offence;
-- src:794 | (b) $1,000.
@ref SSSA2015 s 17(1) (src:785-794)
GIVEN `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 17(1) the greatest sum that may be collected` MEANS
    IF `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2 AT MOST 1000
    THEN `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2
    ELSE 1000

-- src:785 | 17.—(1) The Board, or an officer or employee of the Board who is
-- src:786 | authorised by the Board in writing, may compound any offence under
-- src:787 | this Act that is prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting
-- src:788 | from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence
-- src:789 | a sum not exceeding the lower of the following:
-- src:791 | (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is
-- src:792 | prescribed for the offence;
-- src:794 | (b) $1,000.
@ref SSSA2015 s 17(1) (src:785-794)
GIVEN sum IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) the sum collected is within the greatest sum` MEANS
    IF sum AT MOST `s 17(1) the greatest sum that may be collected` `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a sum not exceeding the lower of the following"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 17(2): on payment of the sum, no further proceedings are to be taken against that person in respect of the offence.
-- src:796 | (2) On payment of the sum of money, no further proceedings are to
-- src:797 | be taken against that person in respect of the offence.
@ref SSSA2015 s 17(2) (src:796-797)
GIVEN `the sum of money has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(2) no further proceedings are to be taken against the person in respect of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the sum of money has been paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar on proceedings comes "On payment of the sum of money"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 17(3): all sums collected under this section must be paid into the Consolidated Fund.
-- src:799 | (3) All sums collected under this section must be paid into the
-- src:800 | Consolidated Fund.
@ref SSSA2015 s 17(3) (src:799-800)
GIVEN `the sum was collected under section 17` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(3) the sum collected must be paid into the Consolidated Fund` MEANS
    IF `the sum was collected under section 17`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "All sums collected under this section"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:799 | (3) All sums collected under this section must be paid into the
-- src:800 | Consolidated Fund.
@ref SSSA2015 s 17(3) (src:799-800)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party under the Act` `An act under the Act`
`s 17(3) duty of the collector` MEANS
    PARTY `the collector of the compounded sum`
    MUST `pay the sum into the Consolidated Fund`

-- EXPECT FULFILLED: paid on day 30 (the text gives no time limit).
#TRACE `s 17(3) duty of the collector` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the collector of the compounded sum` DOES `pay the sum into the Consolidated Fund` AT 30
-- EXPECT PENDING: nothing done by day 100; the duty is still outstanding, not a breach.
#TRACE `s 17(3) duty of the collector` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

§§ `s 18 Conduct of prosecutions`

-- src:802 | Conduct of prosecutions
-- src:804 | 18. Proceedings in respect of any offence under this Act may, with
-- src:805 | the authorisation of the Public Prosecutor, be conducted by an officer
-- src:806 | or employee of the Board who is authorised by the Board in writing to
-- src:807 | conduct such proceedings.
@ref SSSA2015 s 18 (src:802-807)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or employee of the Board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised by the Board in writing to conduct such proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Public Prosecutor has authorised the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18 the officer or employee may conduct the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer or employee of the Board`
       AND `the person is authorised by the Board in writing to conduct such proceedings`
       AND `the Public Prosecutor has authorised the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
