    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 19 Protection from personal liability`

-- s 19(1), (2) and (3): no liability lies personally against the individuals listed
-- who, acting in good faith and with reasonable care, do or omit to do anything in
-- the execution or purported execution of the Act.  The Board and an administrator
-- that is a public authority are not individuals and are not listed; their members,
-- officers and employees are.
-- src:811 | 19.—(1) No liability is to lie personally against any of the
-- src:812 | following individuals who, acting in good faith and with
-- src:813 | reasonable care, does or omits to do anything in the execution or
-- src:814 | purported execution of this Act:
-- src:816 | (a) the Commissioner for Silver Support;
-- src:818 | (b) any Deputy Commissioner for Silver Support;
-- src:820 | (c) any Assistant Commissioner for Silver Support;
-- src:825 | (d) any public officer (or employee of a public authority)
-- src:826 | acting under the Commissioner’s direction;
-- src:828 | (e) any member, officer or employee of the Board;
-- src:830 | (f) any investigator.
-- src:832 | (2) Where an administrator is a public officer, no liability is to lie
-- src:833 | personally against the administrator, or any public officer acting
-- src:834 | under the administrator’s direction, who, acting in good faith and
-- src:835 | with reasonable care, does or omits to do anything in the execution or
-- src:836 | purported execution of this Act.
-- src:838 | (3) Where an administrator is a public authority (other than the
-- src:839 | Board), no liability is to lie personally against any member, officer or
-- src:840 | employee of the administrator who, acting in good faith and with
-- src:841 | reasonable care, does or omits to do anything in the execution or
-- src:842 | purported execution of this Act.
@ref SSSA2015 s 19(1), (2) and (3) (src:811-842)
GIVEN individual IS A Capacity
      `the individual acts in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual acts with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual does or omits to do the thing in the execution or purported execution of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19 no liability lies personally against the individual` MEANS
    IF `the individual is one that section 19 lists`
       AND `the individual acts in good faith`
       AND `the individual acts with reasonable care`
       AND `the individual does or omits to do the thing in the execution or purported execution of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the protection is for the individuals listed "who, acting in good faith and with reasonable care, does or omits to do anything in the execution or purported execution of this Act"
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the individual is one that section 19 lists` MEANS
            individual EQUALS `the Commissioner for Silver Support`
            OR individual EQUALS `a Deputy Commissioner for Silver Support`
            OR individual EQUALS `an Assistant Commissioner for Silver Support`
            OR individual EQUALS `a public officer or employee of a public authority acting under the Commissioner's direction`
            OR individual EQUALS `a member, officer or employee of the Board`
            OR individual EQUALS `an investigator`
            OR individual EQUALS `an administrator who is a public officer`
            OR individual EQUALS `a public officer acting under the direction of an administrator who is a public officer`
            OR individual EQUALS `a member, officer or employee of an administrator that is a public authority other than the Board`

-- s 19(4): "To avoid doubt, this section does not exclude any liability under
-- section 20 of the Financial Procedure Act 1966 or under section 8(6) or 9(7)."
-- src:844 | (4) To avoid doubt, this section does not exclude any liability under
-- src:845 | section 20 of the Financial Procedure Act 1966 or under section 8(6)
-- src:846 | or 9(7).
@ref SSSA2015 s 19(4) (src:844-846)
GIVEN liability IS A `Kind of liability`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(4) section 19 leaves the liability in place` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF liability EQUALS `liability under section 20 of the Financial Procedure Act 1966`
           OR liability EQUALS `liability under section 8(6)`
           OR liability EQUALS `liability under section 9(7)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names three liabilities "To avoid doubt" and says nothing of any other
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 20 Regulations`

-- s 20(1): the Minister may make regulations for carrying out the purposes and provisions of the Act.
-- src:850 | 20.—(1) The Minister may make regulations for carrying out the
-- src:851 | purposes and provisions of this Act.
@ref SSSA2015 s 20(1) (src:850-851)
GIVEN `the regulations are for carrying out the purposes and provisions of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(1) the Minister may make the regulations` MEANS
    IF `the regulations are for carrying out the purposes and provisions of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to make regulations "for carrying out the purposes and provisions of this Act"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 20(2): without limiting s 20(1), regulations may be made for or with respect to the matters (a) to (i).
